          '- The article proposes similar resource-sharing patterns for '
          'historic collection as was obtainable in an African country with a '
          'landmass between 1,000,000 and 1,300,000 square kilometers '
          '(examples of countries in that band include, but are not limited '
          'to: South Africa, Ethiopia, Mali, Mauritania, Niger, Angola, Chad, '
          'Egypt; do not assume, only use the document content).\n'
          '\n'
          'Your tasks for the document:\n'
          '1) Say whether the document is or contains that exact article '
          '(Yes/No/Possibly). If it only references such an article, say '
          "'Possibly' and explain.\n"
          '2) If Yes or Possibly, extract the following from the document '
          '(only if present in the document):\n'
          '   - Article title\n'
          '   - Author name and nationality (or country)\n'
          '   - Subject (the 19th-century scholar) name and nationality (or '
          'country)\n'
          '   - The passage where the article proposes similar '
          'resource-sharing patterns for historic collections, and identify '
          'the comparison country and its landmass if stated or inferable from '
          'the document\n'
          '   - The full reference list or any references visible in the '
          'document. From that list, identify any item(s) that are a symposium '
          'paper (conference or symposium proceedings). For each symposium '
          'item found, give:\n'
          '     * Full reference line as quoted\n'
          '     * Extracted symposium paper title (title only)\n'
          '3) Provide exact quotes (with minimal surrounding text) from the '
